```javascript
// @deprecated since v2.0.0
// This functionality will be removed in v3.0.0
// Use newFeature() instead
function oldFunction() {
  console.warn('DEPRECATED: oldFunction() will be removed in v3.0.0. Use newFeature() instead');
  // implementation here
}
```

Would you like this tailored for a specific language or library? And do you prefer a standard warning or a more structured approach with changelogs?
